<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<model version="NetLogo 7.0.4" snapToGrid="true">
  <code><![CDATA[extensions [
  csv
  profiler
]

globals [
  giving-up-time                                                       ; number of moves without a capture before predator switches back to extensive search
  avg-local-density                                                    ; average number of prey expected in a circle of radius response-radius at start of simulation

  detection-radius                                                     ; distance from which a predator can detect (and capture) prey item
  wall-min                                                             ; lower edge of habitat (in both x and y)
  wall-max                                                             ; upper edge of habitat (in both x and y)

  move-lengths                                                         ; move length (cm = grid units) at each point of cumulative distribution
  ml-extensive                                                         ; list of cumulative frequency for move lengths from extensive mode
  ml-intensive                                                         ; list of cumulative frequency for move lengths from intensive mode

  turn-angles                                                          ; turn angle (degrees) at each point of cumulative distribution
  ta-extensive                                                         ; list of cumulative frequency for turn angles from extensive mode
  ta-intensive                                                         ; list of cumulative frequency for turn angles from intensive mode
]

breed [ prey a-prey ]
breed [ predators predator ]

; predators can detect/capture prey within detection-radius; assume 100% capture probability
predators-own [
  search-mode
  moves-since-capture                                                  ; number of moves since last prey capture
  prey-captured
]

prey-own [
  selected?                                                            ; prey randomly selected for simulation
  present?                                                             ; set to false when prey consumed
  regeneration-tick                                                    ; tick at which a consumed prey item reappears
]

;; SETUP ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

to setup
  clear-all
  if (use-scenario?)[ set-scenarios ]
  set-globals
  ask patches [ set pcolor 99 ]
  set-boundary-patches
  create-prey-grid
  distribute-prey
  add-predator
  reset-ticks
end

to set-scenarios
  let data csv:from-file "InputData/Scenarios.csv"
  let header item 0 data
  let sc item scenario data                                            ; row 0 is header so row index equals scenario number
  set prey-patch-size item (position "PreyPatchSize" header) sc
  set prey-spacing item (position "PreySpacing" header) sc
  set prey-number item (position "PreyNumber" header) sc
end

to set-globals
  set detection-radius 1
  set giving-up-time 10
  ;; habitat is a 70 x 70 square; patches 1-70 are habitat and the outer ring of patches is boundary
  ;; prey sit on lattice points (integer coordinates) 1-70; habitat edges are at 0.5 and 70.5
  set wall-min min-pxcor + 0.5
  set wall-max max-pxcor - 0.5
  set avg-local-density report-avg-local-density
  set-move-lengths
  set-turn-angles
end

to-report report-avg-local-density
  ;; average number of prey that would fall within a circle of radius response-radius
  report prey-number * (pi * response-radius ^ 2) / ((wall-max - wall-min) ^ 2)
end

to set-move-lengths
  ;; reformat data into 3 separate lists (rather than nested lists) for use in calc-piecewise
  let data butfirst csv:from-file "InputData/MoveLength.csv"           ; butfirst drops header row
  set move-lengths map [ x -> item 0 x ] data
  set ml-extensive clean-cdf map [ x -> item 1 x ] data
  set ml-intensive clean-cdf map [ x -> item 2 x ] data
end

to set-turn-angles
  ;; reformat data into 3 separate lists (rather than nested lists) for use in calc-piecewise
  let data butfirst csv:from-file "InputData/TurnAngle.csv"            ; butfirst drops header row
  set turn-angles map [ x -> item 0 x ] data
  set ta-extensive clean-cdf map [ x -> item 1 x ] data
  set ta-intensive clean-cdf map [ x -> item 2 x ] data
end

to-report clean-cdf [ cdf ]
  ;; cumulative frequencies were digitized from Figs 1 and 2 of Hill et al. (2003)
  ;; digitizing error produces small decreases and final values slightly > 1
  ;; force the curve to be non-decreasing and rescale so that it ends at 1
  let running-max 0
  let out []
  foreach cdf [ p ->
    set running-max max list running-max p
    set out lput running-max out
  ]
  report map [ p -> p / last out ] out
end

to set-boundary-patches
  ask patches with [pxcor = min-pxcor or pxcor = max-pxcor or pycor = min-pycor or pycor = max-pycor][ set pcolor black ]
end

to create-prey-grid
  ;; one potential prey item at each lattice point in a square patch at the center of the habitat
  set-default-shape prey "dot"
  let start 1 + floor ((max-pxcor - 1 - prey-patch-size) / 2)
  let grid-pos n-values prey-patch-size [ i -> start + i ]
  foreach grid-pos [ x ->
    foreach grid-pos [ y ->
      create-prey 1 [
        setxy x y
        set color 98
        set size 0.5
        set selected? false
        set present? false
        set regeneration-tick 0
      ]
    ]
  ]
end

to distribute-prey
  ;; randomly select prey-number lattice points subject to minimum spacing between prey;
  ;; candidates closer than or equal to prey-spacing from an already selected prey are excluded
  repeat prey-number [
    let chosen prey with [selected?]
    let candidates prey with [not selected? and not any? chosen with [distance myself <= prey-spacing]]
    if (not any? candidates)[ error "Too many prey for selected patch size and prey spacing" ]
    ask one-of candidates [
      set color 136
      set size 1
      set selected? true
      set present? true
    ]
  ]
  ask prey with [not selected?][ die ]
end

to add-predator
  set-default-shape predators "dot"
  create-predators 1 [
    setxy random-position random-position
    set color brown
    set size 2
    set search-mode "extensive"
    set moves-since-capture 0
    set prey-captured 0
    if (pen-down?)[ pen-down ]                                         ; if true, the forager's path will be traced; visualization purposes only
  ]
end

to-report random-position
  report wall-min + random-float (wall-max - wall-min)
end

;; GO ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; each tick represents one pause: predator looks for prey, decides on next type of move, and moves

to go
  ask prey with [not present? and ticks >= regeneration-tick][ regenerate ]
  ask predators [
    check-prey
    update-search-mode
    move
  ]
  tick
end

to regenerate
  set color 136
  set present? true
end

to check-prey
  ;; prey are only detected during pauses (saltatory search); at most one prey captured per pause
  let target-prey prey with [present? and distance myself <= detection-radius]
  ifelse (any? target-prey)[
    ask min-one-of target-prey [distance myself][
      set color black
      set present? false
      set regeneration-tick ticks + regeneration-time
    ]
    set prey-captured prey-captured + 1
    set moves-since-capture 0
  ][
    set moves-since-capture moves-since-capture + 1
  ]
end

to update-search-mode
  if (search-tactic = "extensive-intensive")[
    ifelse (prey-captured > 0 and moves-since-capture < giving-up-time)[
      set search-mode "intensive"
    ][
      set search-mode "extensive"
    ]
  ]
  if (search-tactic = "local-density")[
    let local-density count prey with [present? and distance myself <= response-radius]
    ifelse (local-density > avg-local-density)[
      set search-mode "intensive"
    ][
      set search-mode "extensive"
    ]
  ]
end

to move
  ifelse (search-tactic = "random-sampling")[
    setxy random-position random-position                              ; randomly relocate predator in virtual tank
  ][
    let dist draw-move-length search-mode
    let turn draw-turn-angle search-mode
    set heading heading + turn
    move-with-reflection dist
  ]
end

to move-with-reflection [ dist ]
  ;; move dist along current heading; reflect off habitat edges (angle of incidence = angle of reflection)
  while [dist > 0][
    let step-x sin heading
    let step-y cos heading
    let tx distance-to-wall xcor step-x
    let ty distance-to-wall ycor step-y
    let d-wall min list tx ty
    ifelse (dist < d-wall)[
      setxy (xcor + dist * step-x) (ycor + dist * step-y)
      set dist 0
    ][
      setxy (clamp (xcor + d-wall * step-x)) (clamp (ycor + d-wall * step-y))
      set dist dist - d-wall
      if (tx <= ty)[ set heading (- heading) ]                          ; hit left or right edge
      if (ty <= tx)[ set heading (180 - heading) ]                      ; hit bottom or top edge (both if corner)
    ]
  ]
end

to-report distance-to-wall [ pos delta ]
  ;; distance along current heading to the edge of habitat in one dimension
  if (delta > 0)[ report max list 0 ((wall-max - pos) / delta) ]
  if (delta < 0)[ report max list 0 ((wall-min - pos) / delta) ]
  report 1e10                                                           ; moving parallel to edge
end

to-report clamp [ pos ]
  report max list wall-min min list wall-max pos
end

to-report draw-move-length [ mode ]
  if (mode = "extensive") [ report calc-piecewise random-float 1 ml-extensive move-lengths ]
  if (mode = "intensive") [ report calc-piecewise random-float 1 ml-intensive move-lengths ]
  error (word "search mode must be extensive or intensive; not " mode)
end

to-report draw-turn-angle [ mode ]
  if (mode = "extensive") [ report calc-piecewise random-float 1 ta-extensive turn-angles ]
  if (mode = "intensive") [ report calc-piecewise random-float 1 ta-intensive turn-angles ]
  error (word "search mode must be extensive or intensive; not " mode)
end

to-report calc-piecewise [#xval #xList #yList]
  ;; linear interpolation; used here to invert the empirical cumulative distributions
  ;; https://stackoverflow.com/questions/50506275/table-functions-interpolation-in-netlogo
  if not (length #xList = length #yList)[ error "mismatched points" ]
  if #xval <= first #xList [ report first #yList ]
  if #xval >= last #xList [ report last #yList ]
  ; binary search for index of first x value that is larger than input x
  let lo 0
  let hi length #xList - 1
  while [hi - lo > 1][
    let mid floor ((lo + hi) / 2)
    ifelse (item mid #xList <= #xval)[ set lo mid ][ set hi mid ]
  ]
  ; get the xy values bracketing the input x
  let xlow item lo #xList
  let xhigh item hi #xList
  let ylow item lo #yList
  let yhigh item hi #yList
  ; interpolate
  report ylow + ( (#xval - xlow) / (xhigh - xlow) ) * ( yhigh - ylow )
end

;; Tests ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

to profile
  setup                  ;; set up the model
  profiler:start         ;; start profiling
  repeat 10000 [ go ]    ;; run something you want to measure
  profiler:stop          ;; stop profiling
  print profiler:report  ;; view the results
  profiler:reset         ;; clear the data
end

to show-response-radius
  ;; helper procedure for 'manually' testing model
  ifelse (search-tactic = "local-density")[
    ask patches with [pcolor = blue][ set pcolor 99 ]
    ask predators[
      ask patches with [pcolor = 99 and distance myself <= response-radius][ set pcolor blue ]
      print count prey with [present? and distance myself <= response-radius]
      print search-mode
    ]
  ][
    print "Did you mean to select local-density as the search-tactic?"
  ]
end

to show-GUT
  ifelse (search-tactic = "extensive-intensive")[
    ask predators [
      print search-mode
      print moves-since-capture
    ]
  ][
    print "Did you mean to select extensive-intensive as the search-tactic?"
  ]
end

to test-corners
  setup
  ask predators [
    setxy 0.6 0.6
    set heading 225
    pen-down
    move-with-reflection 5
    print (list xcor ycor heading)
  ]
end

to test-random-draws
  let ml [["Extensive" "Intensive"]]
  let ta [["Extensive" "Intensive"]]
  repeat 100000 [
    set ml lput (list draw-move-length "extensive" draw-move-length "intensive") ml
    set ta lput (list draw-turn-angle "extensive" draw-turn-angle "intensive") ta
  ]
  csv:to-file "MoveLengthTest.csv" ml
  csv:to-file "TurnAngleTest.csv" ta
  print "done"
end]]></code>
  <widgets>
    <view x="220" wrappingAllowedX="false" y="15" frameRate="30.0" minPycor="0" height="729" showTickCounter="true" patchSize="10.0" fontSize="10" wrappingAllowedY="false" width="728" tickCounterLabel="moves" maxPycor="71" updateMode="1" maxPxcor="71" minPxcor="0"></view>
    <button x="25" y="375" height="33" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="false" kind="Observer" width="66" sizeVersion="0">setup</button>
    <button x="135" y="375" height="33" disableUntilTicks="false" forever="true" kind="Observer" width="63" sizeVersion="0">go</button>
    <switch x="50" y="430" height="33" on="false" variable="pen-down?" display="pen-down?" width="122" sizeVersion="0"></switch>
    <note x="25" y="355" height="26" backgroundDark="0" fontSize="11" width="175" markdown="false" textColorLight="-16777216" backgroundLight="0">-------------------------------------------</note>
    <slider x="20" step="1" y="105" max="70" display="prey-patch-size" height="33" min="5" direction="Horizontal" default="70.0" variable="prey-patch-size" width="172" sizeVersion="0"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="1" y="150" max="10" display="prey-spacing" height="33" min="0" direction="Horizontal" default="7.0" variable="prey-spacing" width="172" sizeVersion="0"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="1" y="195" max="50" display="prey-number" height="33" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="49.0" variable="prey-number" width="172" sizeVersion="0"></slider>
    <slider x="20" step="0.25" y="295" max="9" display="response-radius" height="33" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="9.0" variable="response-radius" width="172" sizeVersion="0"></slider>
    <chooser x="20" y="240" height="45" variable="search-tactic" current="3" display="search-tactic" width="175" sizeVersion="0">
      <choice type="string" value="random-sampling"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="extensive-only"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="extensive-intensive"></choice>
      <choice type="string" value="local-density"></choice>
    </chooser>
    <switch x="35" y="15" height="33" on="true" variable="use-scenario?" display="use-scenario?" width="142" sizeVersion="0"></switch>
    <slider x="20" step="1" y="60" max="26" display="scenario" height="33" min="1" direction="Horizontal" default="26.0" variable="scenario" width="172" sizeVersion="0"></slider>
    <input x="20" multiline="false" y="475" height="60" variable="regeneration-time" type="number" width="172">1000.0</input>
    <monitor x="20" precision="0" y="545" height="60" fontSize="11" width="172" display="prey captured">sum [prey-captured] of predators</monitor>
  </widgets>
  <info><![CDATA[## WHAT IS IT?

A replication of the simulation model of saltatory search by juvenile plaice (*Pleuronectes platessa*) described in Hill, Burrows & Hughes (2003) *Journal of Fish Biology* 63 (Suppl. A): 117–130. A single predator searches a 70 x 70 grid unit habitat (1 grid unit = 1 cm) for prey. Prey sit on lattice points (integer coordinates). The model compares how many prey are captured by four search tactics across 26 artificial prey distributions (Table I in the paper).

## HOW IT WORKS

Each tick is one pause in the predator's search path. During a pause the predator:

1. **Looks for prey.** Prey are only detected during pauses (saltatory search). If any present prey are within `detection-radius` (1 grid unit) of the predator's position, the closest one is captured (100% capture probability, at most one per pause). A captured prey item is absent for `regeneration-time` predator moves and then reappears.
2. **Chooses the type of its next move** (extensive or intensive) according to `search-tactic`:
   - **random-sampling**: the predator is relocated to a random position each tick. This is the baseline used to calculate relative efficiency.
   - **extensive-only**: every move is extensive.
   - **extensive-intensive**: the 10 moves after a capture (the giving-up time) are intensive; all others are extensive.
   - **local-density**: the next move is intensive if the number of present prey within `response-radius` (9 or 4.5 in the paper) of the predator exceeds the average number expected in a circle of that size (`prey-number * pi * response-radius ^ 2 / 70 ^ 2`); otherwise it is extensive.
3. **Moves.** It turns by a random angle and then moves a random distance. Both are drawn from the empirical cumulative distributions for extensive or intensive search (Figs 1 and 2 of the paper; `InputData/MoveLength.csv` and `InputData/TurnAngle.csv`). The predator reflects off the edges of the habitat.

Prey distributions are generated by placing `prey-number` prey at random lattice points within a square patch of side `prey-patch-size` at the center of the habitat. No two prey may be within `prey-spacing` grid units of each other.

## HOW TO USE IT

Turn on `use-scenario?` and pick a `scenario` (1–26) to use the prey distributions in Table I (`InputData/Scenarios.csv`). Turn it off to set `prey-patch-size`, `prey-spacing` and `prey-number` directly. Choose a `search-tactic` (and `response-radius` for local-density), then press setup and go. Turn on `pen-down?` to trace the predator's path.

The BehaviorSpace experiments reproduce the simulation design in the paper: 60 runs of 1,000,000 moves for each combination of tactic and scenario. Run them headlessly with `run-experiments.sh` and summarise the results with `Analysis/analysis.R`.

## THINGS TO NOTICE

The paper states that captured prey were absent for 1000 predator moves. With that value, random sampling captures many fewer prey than shown in Fig. 3 of the paper (e.g., ~19,000 vs ~31,000 per million moves for 49 prey in the homogeneous habitat). The published values are reproduced almost exactly when prey are not depleted (`regeneration-time` = 1). The experiments therefore include both values. See the README for a comparison with the published results.

## IMPLEMENTATION NOTES

Points where the paper is ambiguous and the choices made here:

- The predator's position is continuous (double precision rather than the 10^-5 grid unit resolution in the paper). Detection and local density are measured from the predator's exact position.
- Local density is counted after any capture in the current pause and determines the next move.
- A patch of side *s* contains *s* x *s* lattice points, so habitat homogeneity = *s*² / 70² as in Table I.
- Prey spacing excludes candidate lattice points at a distance less than or equal to `prey-spacing` from an existing prey item. This keeps a spacing of 1 meaningful on an integer lattice.
- The cumulative distributions were digitized from the published figures. Small digitizing errors (slight decreases and final values above 1) are removed by forcing each curve to be non-decreasing and rescaling it to end at 1. Values are drawn by linear interpolation of the inverse cumulative distribution.
- The natural prey distributions (Table II, Fig. 5) are not included because the field maps are not available.

## CREDITS AND REFERENCES

Hill, S. L., Burrows, M. T. & Hughes, R. N. (2003). The efficiency of adaptive search tactics for different prey distribution patterns: a simulation model based on the behaviour of juvenile plaice. *Journal of Fish Biology* 63 (Suppl. A), 117–130. https://doi.org/10.1111/j.1095-8649.2003.00212.x

Code hosted on [GitHub](https://github.com/hinkelman/plaice-search-model).]]></info>
